response:
The tests are calling `meetup(year, month, week, day)`, but the current implementation expects `meetup(year, month, day, week)`. That causes the weekday lookup to receive values like `"teenth"` or `"first"`, resulting in `Invalid day`.

The fix is to swap the `week` and `day` parameters.

meetup.js
```
export const meetup = (year, month, week, day) => {
  const dayOfWeek = {
    Sunday: 0,
    Monday: 1,
    Tuesday: 2,
    Wednesday: 3,
    Thursday: 4,
    Friday: 5,
    Saturday: 6,
  };

  const startDay = {
    first: 1,
    second: 8,
    third: 15,
    fourth: 22,
    teenth: 13,
  };

  const targetDay = dayOfWeek[day];
  if (targetDay === undefined) {
    throw new Error('Invalid day');
  }

  if (week === 'last') {
    const date = new Date(year, month, 0);
    while (date.getDay() !== targetDay) {
      date.setDate(date.getDate() - 1);
    }
    return date;
  }

  const firstCandidate = startDay[week];
  if (firstCandidate === undefined) {
    throw new Error('Invalid week');
  }

  const date = new Date(year, month - 1, firstCandidate);
  while (date.getDay() !== targetDay) {
    date.setDate(date.getDate() + 1);
  }

  return date;
};
```
